# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is git-ignored and must stay that way.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHICH DATABASE
#
# There are two Supabase projects and this file decides which one you talk to.
# For local development that must be the DEVELOPMENT project. Point it at
# production and every post you write while testing is a post a student can
# read — which is how it worked until Phase 4B, and why this warning exists.
#
# The app checks: a non-production build holding the production project ref
# turns the badge beside the wordmark red and logs a console warning. If you see
# PROD DATA there, stop and fix this file. See DATABASE.md → Environments.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase — Project Settings → API, in the DEVELOPMENT project (1elevate-dev).
# The NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are sent to the browser on purpose; they grant nothing
# on their own, because row-level security still applies to whoever the access
# token says you are.
#
# Supabase renamed these: the publishable key is what newer projects are given,
# the anon key is what older ones have. Set whichever your dashboard shows —
# the app reads both names, newest first.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The counterpart secret (newer projects: "secret key"; older: "service_role").
# It bypasses every row-level policy. Server-side only — never prefix it with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, never import it from a "use client" file. Leave it empty unless
# something actually needs it; nothing in the app does today.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# The AI tutor and the question generator. Without it those two features return
# a clear message and everything else works as usual.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to claude-opus-5.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: force the environment label.
#
# Normally left unset. Locally the app infers "development" from NODE_ENV, and on
# Vercel it reads NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ENV, which is already correct for both the
# production deployment and every preview. Set this only to override that —
# for instance to see what a preview build's badge looks like from localhost.
#
# One of: development | preview | production
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not used by the app — used by the Supabase CLI, and only if you run
# migrations. A personal access token from
# https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens
#
# Keep it out of this repo. Prefer `npx supabase login`, which stores it in your
# own user profile, over putting it in .env.local at all.
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Desmos graphing calculator, used in the Math sections. Optional: without a key
# the app uses Desmos's public demo key, which is for evaluation only — read
# DESMOS.md before this is in front of students. Public by design; Desmos
# restricts a key by domain rather than by secrecy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DESMOS_API_KEY=
# Optional. Defaults to v1.11.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DESMOS_VERSION=
